-- title:
--   Compositum of the function fields of X₁(Nt) and X(Γ₁(N)∩Γ₀(Nq))
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, and let $N$, $t$, $q$ be nonzero natural numbers with $t$ and $q$ coprime; let $N'$ be a natural number with $N' = Nt$. For a congruence subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and a field $K$, write $F_K(\Gamma)$ for [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), the intermediate field of the Laurent series field `LaurentSeries K` obtained by adjoining to $K$ the set `intFormRatiosC K Γ` attached to $\Gamma$; thus `x1FunctionFieldC K M` is $F_K(\Gamma_1(M))$, `x1FunctionField M` is $F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_1(M))$, and `x1x0FunctionFieldC K M t` is $F_K(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(t))$. For an intermediate field $F_0$ of `LaurentSeries ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$, `laurentBaseChange L F₀` is the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries L` over $L$ generated by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise ring homomorphism induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. The assertion is the equality, in the lattice of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries L` over $L$, of the join of the base changes of $F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_1(N'))$ and of $F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_1(N) \cap \Gamma_0(Nq))$ with the base change of $F_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Gamma_1(N') \cap \Gamma_0(N'q))$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the group-theoretic identity $\Gamma_1(Nt) \cap (\Gamma_1(N) \cap \Gamma_0(Nq)) = \Gamma_1(Nt) \cap \Gamma_0(Ntq)$ for $\gcd(t,q) = 1$, expressed through the Galois correspondence for modular function fields over a coefficient field $L$ of characteristic zero. It supplies the generation statement used in [`ModularCurve.JOne.degeneracyPullbackPair_comm_heckeOperatorOneBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JOne.degeneracyPullbackPair_comm_heckeOperatorOneBar), where the roof of the degree-$q$ Hecke correspondence at level $Nt$ must be recognised as the compositum of the function field of $X_1(Nt)$ with the corresponding roof at level $N$.
